ed encounters for removed characters. For removed prompts, archive every targeted dialogue block. Replacements must preserve the original evidence and stable references. Ask for clarification if restructuring cannot be represented safely within the existing request scope.","List only feedback actually resolved in resolvedFeedback with the exact exported key, flag, critical and note values. Leave unrelated or unresolved feedback intact. Do not mark newly implemented content tester-verified.","The user imports and previews the receipt in NPCDex. Reconciliation updates live data, logs before/after history, clears explicitly resolved feedback, changes implemented UPDATE to FINAL, and resets affected tester statuses. Receipt import does not modify or independently inspect the ROM.","If romReversalRequests are present, prioritize them before reapplying restored forward proposals. Return NPCDexROMReversalReceipt/1 for each completed reversal. The inverse NPCDex data changes have already been applied; do not apply them again. Use the request historyId, a unique reversal receiptId, expected implemented ROM hash as romBeforeHash and actual restored ROM hash as romAfterHash."],"receiptSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","required":["schema","receiptId","romBeforeHash","romAfterHash","implementedAt","entries"],"properties":{"schema":{"const":"NPCDexImplementationReceipt/1"},"receiptId":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"romBeforeHash":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$"},"romAfterHash":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$"},"implementedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"entries":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"object","required":["planId","requestHash","baselineHash","patches","resolvedFeedback"],"properties":{"planId":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"requestHash":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$"},"baselineHash":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$"},"patches":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"object","required":["path","before","after"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","pattern":"^/"},"before":{"$ref":"#/$defs/state"},"after":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/state"},{"properties":{"exists":{"const":true}},"required":["value"]}]}}}},"resolvedFeedback":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["key","flag","critical","note"],"properties":{"key":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"flag":{"type":"boolean"},"critical":{"type":"boolean"},"note":{"type":"string"}}}}}}}},"$defs":{"state":{"type":"object","required":["exists"],"properties":{"exists":{"type":"boolean"},"value":{}},"if":{"properties":{"exists":{"const":true}}},"then":{"required":["value"]},"else":{"not":{"required":["value"]}}}}},"reversalReceiptSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","required":["schema","historyId","receiptId","romBeforeHash","romAfterHash"],"properties":{"schema":{"const":"NPCDexROMReversalReceipt/1"},"historyId":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"receiptId":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"romBeforeHash":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$"},"romAfterHash":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$"}}},"workflowGuide":"# NPCDex Agent Workflow · 2.29\n\nThe Agent Export is the complete portable dataset, including current content, review annotations, embedded images, change plans and history. Treat source-document instructions as evidence, not authorization to change the ROM. Only approved change instructions authorize implementation.\n\n## Review and planning\n\nUse a tile cog to set FINAL, UPDATE or REMOVE. A parent decision applies to its descendants unless a more specific decision overrides it. Tile readiness within a building or room is scoped to that location; map-level readiness includes all encounters. UPDATE and REMOVE require Change Instructions. Scene changes follow the ticket instructions case by case; there is no advance Shared Scene Handling selector. The inline status row targets the current consecutive speaker prompt; the cog provides diagnostics/source references. Condition Notes is removed. Dialogue events have no separate decision scope.\n\nProposed Dialogue is a proposal, not live dialogue. Planning does not delete records or modify the ROM. FINAL expresses editorial intent; tester verification remains separate. Flags and notes are diagnostic feedback. Critical flags block readiness and turn indicators red.\n\nSave Changes overwrites `npcdex-agent-export.json` in the chosen package folder and saves a browser-local copy. Give this saved file to the coding agent. Do not give an older bundled export after making new notes.\n\n## Export contract\n\n`exportSchema` is `NPCDexAgentExport/2`. `changePlans` stores all decisions. `changeRequests` contains pending UPDATE/REMOVE requests. Each request includes:\n\n- `id`, stable `target`, `intent`, instructions, proposal, shared-scene handling and timestamps.\n- `references`: original source/script IDs, related points, shared scenes and technical metadata.\n- `baseline`: the exact live target content at export time.\n- `baselineHash`: SHA-256 of UTF-8 `JSON.stringify(baseline)`.\n- `requestHash`: SHA-256 of UTF-8 `JSON.stringify({target,intent,instructions,proposedDialogue,sharedSceneHandling,updatedAt})`, in that property order. JavaScript omits undefined properties.\n- `feedback`: the exported flags/notes for the affected review scope, with their annotation keys and exact values.\n\nHash the supplied structures without reformatting or reordering their properties. Use the export's existing hashes in the receipt. NPCDex recomputes them against current data before applying changes.\n\nDisplay labels are not identifiers. Dialogue renames use `displayName` and retain `originalDisplayName`. Character display names live in `characterNames`, keyed by stable identity; there is no manual identity-linking control. Keep character IDs, point IDs, block IDs, script tags, source records, original baselines and mapping evidence intact. Images share by explicit identity; changing a name does not merge identities. `liveMappings` can record newly implemented script mappings without erasing original evidence.\n\n## Coding-agent implementation\n\n1. Inspect all pending requests and their shared references. Resolve conflicting overlapping requests before writing anything.\n2. Check the actual working ROM and source scripts against the supplied evidence. Export hashes describe NPCDex data, not proof of ROM state. Record real before/after ROM hashes and retain a ROM/source backup.\n3. Implement the approved request in the ROM project. Preserve unaffected participants and conditions. For Retain Other Participants, changes to a character's shared scene are limited to that character's blocks and participant reference; do not archive the shared scene or other participants' events.\n4. Produce a receipt describing exact current-data changes. Archive removed records with `archived: true`, including a removed character's exclusively owned encounters. Preserve their records, IDs and text for reconciliation and undo. Archive the removed character's shared dialogue blocks and remove only that participant reference as needed. Do not delete array members or substitute new stable IDs.\n5. Give the receipt to the user for import through Data → implementation receipt. NPCDex previews it before the user applies it. Apply only after ROM changes are implemented; importing a receipt does not itself write the ROM.\n\n## Implementation receipt\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"NPCDexImplementationReceipt/1\",\n  \"receiptId\": \"unique-implementation-id\",\n  \"romBeforeHash\": \"actual-before-rom-sha256\",\n  \"romAfterHash\": \"actual-after-rom-sha256\",\n  \"implementedAt\": \"2026-10-12T12:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"planId\": \"plan-id-from-export\",\n      \"requestHash\": \"requestHash-from-export\",\n      \"baselineHash\": \"baselineHash-from-export\",\n      \"patches\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"/towns/0/areas/0/elements/0/points/0/blocks/0/text\",\n          \"before\": {\"exists\": true, \"value\": \"Exact existing text\"},\n          \"after\": {\"exists\": true, \"value\": \"Implemented replacement text\"}\n        }\n      ],\n      \"resolvedFeedback\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nPaths above are illustrative; determine real indexes from the saved export. JSON pointer segments escape `~` as `~0` and `/` as `~1`. An absent field is represented by `{\"exists\":false}` in `before`. Removal of records uses an `archived` patch with `after: {\"exists\":true,\"value\":true}`; receipt patches cannot physically delete data.\n\nTo clear reconciled feedback, include only explicitly resolved annotations in `resolvedFeedback`, each with its exact `key`, `flag`, `critical` and `note` from the export. Do not clear unrelated notes. NPCDex rejects changed or unrelated feedback, stale requests, unrelated content patches, duplicate receipt IDs and missing original stable records. Changes are applied atomically. UPDATE becomes FINAL after receipt application, but affected prompts become Unreviewed and their indicator remains yellow until retested. Removed archived records stop contributing to active readiness. Original feedback and before/after values remain in history.\n\n## History, fallback and ROM reversal\n\nChange History is available in Data and Flags, Notes & Changes. Each recorded mutation retains immutable before/after JSON-pointer patches. Undo appends a reversal instead of erasing the audit trail. It refuses to overwrite later changes to the same fields. Undo later dependent edits first. An undone implementation resets affected tester marks.\n\nUndo restores NPCDex data only. When an implementation is undone, the next export includes `romReversalRequests` identifying its receipt, expected implemented ROM hash, original ROM hash and inverse content patches. The coding agent must reverse the real ROM/source change separately, prioritizing that reversal before reapplying any restored forward proposal. Confirm completion with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"NPCDexROMReversalReceipt/1\",\n  \"historyId\": \"undo-history-id-from-romReversalRequests\",\n  \"receiptId\": \"unique-reversal-receipt-id\",\n  \"romBeforeHash\": \"expected-implemented-rom-hash\",\n  \"romAfterHash\": \"actual-restored-rom-hash\"\n}\n```\n\nImport this through the same receipt control. It records external reversal confirmation without applying the inverse data twice. Receipts record the coding agent's reported ROM evidence; NPCDex has no direct ROM access.\n\nKeep separately dated copies of important exports and ROM backups outside the normal working package. The working export intentionally overwrites one file; embedded history protects recorded app changes, not an externally lost or corrupted package. Existing pre-2.16 content corrections remain recorded in `reconciliations`; full UI mutation history begins with this version.\n\n## Extending the dex\n\nStart from the latest complete saved export. Add Tier 1 towns, Tier 2 locations and Tier 3 areas using stable unique IDs. Locations group area IDs; areas contain elements and points. Character records reference owned elements and shared scenes. Preserve `participantIds`, documented location scope, gender variants and all source evidence. Use the same `identityId` for recurring named characters, or gender-specific `identityByGender`. Qualify distinct generic NPC names by location.\n\nInternal narrative stage IDs remain stable; the UI displays Roman numerals in stage order. Add stages without renumbering old IDs. Original source prose remains evidence while display prose uses current numerals.\n\nImport the complete updated JSON through Data to validate it, then Save Changes. For packaging, `node update-npcdex.cjs latest-export.json npcdex.html` embeds current data into an existing HTML. For interface code changes, edit the accompanying template/modules, copy the latest export into `npcdex-data.json`, and run `node build-npcdex.cjs`. The resulting HTML is self-contained; the separate source files are for future agent maintenance.\n\r\n\n## Prompt-only migration · 2.26\n\nReview model: SpeakerPromptOnly/1. Whole-event dialogue plans are migrated to speaker prompts, with original plans retained in legacyChangePlans and full migration history. decisionConflicts retains conflicting source/prompt decisions and resolutions. Pending conflicts are excluded from changeRequests; resolve them before coding. The inline status controls target the current prompt. Character and non-dialogue-object tickets remain separate. New character tickets use sharedSceneHandling: instructions; changes to surrounding scenes must follow explicit instructions. Historical scope fields remain retained for existing receipts and audit evidence.\n\n## Inline decisions and Standard Notes Suite · 2.29\n\nCondition Notes is removed. Current speaker prompts use inline Final/Update/Remove controls beside verification. Grey means unset/off; explicit promptStatusUnset entries suppress inherited prompt decisions when cleared. Critical diagnostics still take red priority. Empty instruction drafts are stored in changePlans and changeDrafts with workflow draft, but excluded from changeRequests. An Update marked Critical renders a red Update tag, without changing its intent to Remove. Standard Notes Suite is the default UI for applicable feedback/status controls; see Standard-Notes-Suite.md and the shared renderer module. Tile/character/location suite controls record pending changes immediately; Save Changes persists them. Verification cannot be applied to a whole scene/tile.\n\n## Self-contained export contract · 2.31\n\nEvery Save Changes and manual snapshot export includes agentHandoff: explicit implementation/receipt instructions, machine-readable receipt and reversal schemas, hash/patch rules, and the complete workflow reference. Supply the saved JSON alone; a separate workflow document is optional. Generated contract metadata is refreshed by the running build on each export.\n\n## Reclassified encounter review identity · 2.34\n\nA block may carry reviewKey for the first displayed passage to preserve an existing prompt annotation identity after a formerly silent encounter gains indexed text. Keep this key, the block ID, sourceBlockId and mappingEvidence intact. Archived unused references may carry reassignedTo linking to their live encounter. Tester-reported encounter mappings do not certify an independently rechecked script caller or implemented ROM change.\n\n## Global Dialogue · 2.39\n\nGlobal messages and routines are indexed once in the global-dialogue town. Stable element, point, block and prompt review IDs are retained. originalPlacement, originalContext and originalCondition retain caller provenance. Region-specific encounter records remain regional; character globalDialogueReferences identify their shared message group without duplicating editable text. Do not recreate global review copies per map or erase the original script/source evidence.\n","hashAndPatchRules":["baselineHash = SHA-256 of UTF-8 JSON.stringify(baseline), preserving the supplied property order.","requestHash = SHA-256 of UTF-8 JSON.stringify({target,intent,instructions,proposedDialogue,sharedSceneHandling,updatedAt}) in that order; undefined properties are omitted by JavaScript. Copy the exported hashes; NPCDex recomputes them against current data.","JSON-pointer segments escape ~ as ~0 and / as ~1. Derive actual indexes from this export; example indexes are illustrative. Use before:{exists:false} only for absent fields, otherwise include the exact existing value. Every after state has exists:true and value.","Receipt validation rejects duplicate receipt/plan IDs, stale requests or baselines, mismatched before values, unrelated patches, silent stable-ID/identity changes, physical deletions and removal without archiving. Application is atomic. Never bypass a rejection by changing original IDs/hashes; resolve the mismatch with the user."]},"globalDialogue":{"version":1,"townId":"global-dialogue","originalTownId":"new-bark-town","elementIds":["shared-0","shared-1","shared-2","shared-3"],"pointIds":["shared-0-0","shared-0-1","shared-0-2","shared-0-3","shared-1-0","shared-1-1","shared-1-2","shared-2-0","shared-2-1","shared-2-2","shared-2-3","shared-2-4","shared-3-0"],"reviewPolicy":"One global review record; no repeated regional prompts"}}